---
layout: base.njk
title: Data
extraScripts:
  - /assets/js/papaparse.min.js
  - /assets/js/xlsx.full.min.js
extraBodyScripts:
  - /assets/js/data-list.js
---
<div class="container">
<div class="card-body">
  <div class="d-flex flex-row bd-highlight mb-3">
    <div style="margin-right:1em;">
      <h2>Your Datasets</h2>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    Upload a CSV or Excel file to explore it and build a causal study. Your
    data is processed entirely in your browser and stored locally on this
    device &mdash; it's never uploaded anywhere. See
    <a href="/articles/dataset/" target="_blank">what a Dataset is</a> and
    <a href="/articles/exploratory-analysis/" target="_blank">how to explore your data</a>
    for background.
  </p>

  <div class="card card-body mb-4">
    <h5>Upload a new dataset</h5>
    <form id="upload-form">
      <div class="mb-3">
        <label for="dataset-name" class="form-label">Name</label>
        <input type="text" class="form-control" id="dataset-name" placeholder="e.g. Sales 2024" />
      </div>
      <div class="mb-3">
        <label for="dataset-file" class="form-label">File (CSV or Excel)</label>
        <input type="file" class="form-control" id="dataset-file" accept=".csv,.txt,.xlsx,.xls" />
        <div class="form-text">
          Large files: CSV is processed in the background and stays
          responsive. Excel files are read in one go and may briefly freeze
          the page for very large workbooks &mdash; CSV is recommended above
          a hundred thousand rows or so.
        </div>
      </div>
      <button type="submit" class="btn btn-success" id="upload-button">Upload</button>
      <span id="upload-status" class="ms-2"></span>
    </form>
  </div>

  <div id="dataset-list-empty" class="alert alert-secondary" hidden>
    No datasets yet &mdash; upload one above to get started.
  </div>

  <table class="table" id="dataset-table" hidden>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Name</th>
        <th>Rows</th>
        <th>Columns</th>
        <th>Modified</th>
        <th></th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody id="dataset-table-body"></tbody>
  </table>
</div>
</div>

<div class="modal fade" id="delete-modal" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="modal-dialog">
    <div class="modal-content">
      <div class="modal-header">
        <h5 class="modal-title">Delete dataset?</h5>
        <button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal"></button>
      </div>
      <div class="modal-body">
        <p>This removes <strong id="delete-modal-name"></strong> and its data from this browser. This can't be undone.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="modal-footer">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Cancel</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-danger" id="delete-modal-confirm">Delete</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
